    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Mia, how are snowflakes made?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "❄️",
          "label": "Snowflake"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "☁️",
          "label": "Made how?"
        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "High up in a freezing cold cloud! It starts with a tiny speck of dust floating in the air.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "☁️",
        "text": "In a freezing cloud",
        "cue": "cloud",
        "sub": "Around a speck of dust",
        "sub_cue": "speck"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Water in the cloud freezes onto that speck and makes a teeny ice crystal.",
      "punch": "crystal",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧊",
        "text": "A tiny ice crystal",
        "cue": "crystal"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How does it get so big and pretty?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "As it floats and tumbles, more water freezes onto it, bit by bit. It grows arms, and the arms grow branches!",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "A flake grows",
        "traveler": "❄️",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "☁️",
            "label": "In the cloud",
            "cue": "floats"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💧",
            "label": "Water freezes",
            "cue": "water"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧊",
            "label": "Grows arms",
            "cue": "arms"
          },
          {
            "icon": "❄️",
            "label": "Branches",
            "cue": "branches"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why do snowflakes have six sides?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Because of how teeny bits of water fit together when they freeze. They line up in a six-sided pattern, so the snowflake grows that way too.",
      "punch": "six",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❄️",
        "text": "Six sides!",
        "cue": "six",
        "sub": "Water freezes in a pattern",
        "sub_cue": "pattern"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Are all snowflakes the same?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Nope! Each one takes its own bumpy trip through the cloud, where it can be colder or wetter. That changes how it grows.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌬️",
        "text": "Each has its own trip",
        "cue": "trip",
        "sub": "Colder? Wetter? New shape!",
        "sub_cue": "colder"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "That's why scientists think it's very, very unlikely that two big snowflakes are ever exactly alike!",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔍",
        "text": "No two exactly alike?",
        "cue": "alike"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "And when they get heavy enough, they drift down to the ground as snow.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🌨️",
        "text": "Then they drift down!",
        "cue": "drift",
        "sub": "Hello, snow!",
        "sub_cue": "snow"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "A speck of dust, freezing water, six sides, and every one is different. Wow!",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "icon": "🟤",
            "text": "Speck of dust",
            "cue": "dust"
          },
          {
